A||||3||jd2m4||Do you guys think $130.00 is a good price for a rebuildable 2.8?||||5||
Z||000000||jd2m4||12-06-2001||11:22 PM||||I found a couple of 2.8 engines at the junkyard today,They run,But they need rings,Have a warped head,e.t.c.,So they are being sold as non-running cores,you can buy one complete for $130.00(wireing harness is also included)Do you guys think that's a good price? I had wanted to build up a v-6 anyway,So this is right up my alley.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-07-2001||01:27 AM||||Yes, as long as there are no cracks in the heads and/or block.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||stingant0||12-07-2001||01:35 AM||||I'm doing a rebuild on an 88 formula. I spent $150 on new main bearnings, rod bearings, and pistion rings. The crank at advance auto was about $216 for both the 2.8 and the 3.1 crank. I got the crank turned for about $180. I need to get oversized main bearings now. Plan on spending 2x as much then you think. Oh the heads are around $150 for iron and $250 for Al. BEWARE of exhaust leaks...Nothing worse then an exhaust leak in the rear or front whatever..the firewall side.||||reg||1
